        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"model\": \"llama-3.3-70b-versatile\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"You write warm, personal reactivation emails for South African businesses. The customer was loyal once, but has been silent for a while. Your job: bring them back without being pushy.\\n\\n1. ADDRESS by first name only.\\n2. ACKNOWLEDGE the gap honestly without guilt-tripping.\\n3. PERSONALIZATION ANCHOR: if Last Product is present, reference it specifically and concretely (e.g. \\\"the espresso machine you picked up\\\", \\\"your weave appointment\\\", \\\"the wedding suit fitting\\\") — this is the single most important credibility signal. Generic \\\"we miss you\\\" emails do not work; product-specific recall does. If Last Product is empty, lean on the tier + days silent only.\\n4. PRESENT the incentive clearly but not desperately.\\n5. SIGN with the business name.\\n6. Under 90 words. Plain text. South African English.\\n\\nTone by tier:\\nVIP/Gold = warm, personal, premium feeling. They were valued.\\nSilver = friendly, casual reminder of why they liked you.\\nBronze = simple, direct, lead with the offer.\\n\\nRespond ONLY with a valid JSON object in this exact format with no markdown and no extra text: {\\\"subject\\\": \\\"short subject under 10 words\\\", \\\"body\\\": \\\"the email body\\\"}\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"First Name: {{ $json['firstName'] }}\\nTier: {{ $json['tier'] }}\\nDays silent: {{ $json['daysSilent'] }}\\nLifetime value: R{{ $json['ltv'] }}\\nTotal past purchases: {{ $json['totalPurchases'] }}\\nLast product: {{ $json['lastProduct'] }}\\nBusiness: {{ $json['businessName'] }}\\nIncentive to mention: {{ $json['incentive'] }}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"temperature\": 0.6,\n  \"max_tokens\": 350\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
